ce:section.ce:para:
Fig. 6
 reports the crystallinity and hydrophilicity of membranes. Compared with pristine M membrane, adding GO, BPA-GO, and TSD-GO decreased the d-spacing of the polyimide membrane. This was probably because of strong intermolecular forces between the particle and the polyimide structure. However, adding TTSD-GO in the polyimide membrane enhanced the d-spacing from 5.75 to 5.77 Å. This pertains that the bulky structure of TTSD makes the d-spacing of TTSD-GO@M membrane large. Furthermore, the spectra of particles was not detected on XRD spectra of the membrane because the particles were exfoliated (
   Figure S14
). The surface hydrophilicity of membranes was similar, where the water contact angle of membranes ranged from 84.5 to 87.9°. This indicated that GO was embedded in the bulk of polyimide, and it might affect only the intermolecular interactions within polyimide and the overall free volume in membranes. Thus, PALS analysis (Fig. 7
) was conducted.
